{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-78957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int 9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-78957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=9{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 9{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=3{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot 3{x}^{3}-\\int 3{x}^{3}(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{x}^{3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-78957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95"} {"question" "q-78957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-78957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C"] ["math" "3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{x}^{3}+C"] ["math" "9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3{x}^{3}+C"] ["math" "9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3{x}^{3}+C"] ["math" "{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-78957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{x}^{3}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-78883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}9\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-78883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=9\\sqrt{x} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 9\\sqrt{x}\\,dx=6{x}^{3/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}9\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(6{x}^{3/2}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{6{x}^{3/2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})(6{({e}^{2})}^{3/2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1(6(1)^{3/2})]-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}6\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12{e}^{3}-4{x}^{3/2}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =12{e}^{3}-(4{({e}^{2})}^{3/2}-4(1)^{3/2}) \\\\  & =12{e}^{3}-4{e}^{3}+4 \\\\  & =8{e}^{3}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-78883" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95"} {"question" "q-78883" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-78883" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12{e}^{3}+4"] ["math" "12{e}^{3}-4"] ["math" "4{e}^{3}-4"] ["math" "8{e}^{3}+4"] ["math" "8{e}^{3}-12"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-78883" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8{e}^{3}+4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-350964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}7{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-350964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}) & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=7{x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 7{x}^{2}\\,dx=\\frac{7{x}^{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}7{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})(\\frac{7{x}^{3}}{3}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}(\\frac{7{x}^{3}}{3})(\\frac{2}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{7({e}^{3})^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(({e}^{3})^{2})}{3}-\\frac{7(1)^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡((1)^{2})}{3}]-\\frac{14}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7{e}^{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{6})}{3}-\\frac{14{x}^{3}}{9}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =14{e}^{9}-(\\frac{14{e}^{9}}{9}-\\frac{14}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(126{e}^{9}-14{e}^{9}+14) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{9}(8{e}^{9}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-350964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95"} {"question" "q-350964" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-350964" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{112}{9}e^9+\\frac{14}{9}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (x+7)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x+7\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int (x+7)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+7x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+7)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+7x)-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+7x)(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int x\\text{d}x-7\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{x}{4}-7{x}^{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+7x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7{x}^{2}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-12573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2}+7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-7x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-49716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-49716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,dx=-\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{4}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{4}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{4}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(-\\frac{1}{x}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{4}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{4}}(-\\frac{1}{x})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{4})(-\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)(-\\frac{1}{1})]+{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{{e}^{4}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\frac{1}{x}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{{e}^{4}}-(\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  & =1-5{e}^{-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-49716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95"} {"question" "q-49716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-49716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1-4{e}^{-5}"] ["math" "1-5{e}^{-4}"] ["math" "1-5{e}^{4}"] ["math" "4{e}^{5}+1"] ["math" "5{e}^{-4}+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-49716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1-5{e}^{-4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-12570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-12570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})-\\int (-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-12570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95"} {"question" "q-12570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-12570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-12570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{log}_{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{2}⁡(x)(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡(x)}{2}-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{8}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}})-\\int (-\\frac{2}{{x}^{4}})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{4}}+2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{4}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{2{x}^{4}}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95"} {"question" "q-114557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{4}}+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-3}{{x}^{4}}+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{2{x}^{4}}+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2}{{x}^{4}}+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1}{4{x}^{4}}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114557" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{2{x}^{4}}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int 8{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=8{x}^{3}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 8{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 8{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\cdot (2{x}^{4})-\\int \\frac{2{x}^{4}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}+C \\\\  & ={x}^{4}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{2})+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95"} {"question" "q-114555" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114555" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}^{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+1)+C"] ["math" "{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{3})+C"] ["math" "{x}^{4}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{2})+C"] ["math" "{x}^{4}(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{3}-1)+C"] ["math" "{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114555" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{4}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{2})+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{4}⁡(2x)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}})-\\int (-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{4}⁡(2x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114556" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95"} {"question" "q-114556" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114556" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)-1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114556" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)+1}{9{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+x+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+x+C"] ["math" "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C"] ["math" "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-\\frac{x}{3}+C"] ["math" "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{2}{2x+1} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int \\frac{2x}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use a substitution $2x+1=u,$ thus $2x=u-1$ and $\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int (\\frac{2x}{2x+1})\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\int \\frac{u-1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\,\\text{d}u+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{u}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{u}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡u}{2}+D] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-\\frac{2x+1}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{2}+D] \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=D-\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95"} {"question" "q-114585" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114585" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)+3x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-x}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)+2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114585" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+1)-2x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-346521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-346521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4x\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}-{\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4x)\\,(x){|}_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}-{\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{3}}{4})\\,(\\frac{{e}^{3}}{4})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4})\\,(\\frac{1}{4})]-{\\int }_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-x{|}_{1/4}^{{e}^{3}/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(2{e}^{3}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-346521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95"} {"question" "q-346521" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-346521" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{e^3}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-78969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int 2{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-78969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int 2{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 2\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-78969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95"} {"question" "q-78969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-78969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-78969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/3}^{e}-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x){|}_{1/3}^{e}-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-x{|}_{1/3}^{e}\\, \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-(e-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+e-e+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7f007e4d35389d9b739a877bdebd629961f7f4c5f44fdefff4a6860a90b66c95"} {"question" "q-114597" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114597" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+3e"] ["math" "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+1"] ["math" "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\frac{1}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "q-114597" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "70344e529e45a9479d5e26bc805ecf21484c7a8a20834820d3ddb4b9641a8478"} {"question" "e-493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e} 4x\\ln\\left(x^3\\right) \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/example-493.json" "file_sha256" "ba7bdd5687966781ee367005e519423e48d49430fb7c40f037f14d301011c492"} {"question" "e-493" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and $v',$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x=2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot (2{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}(2{x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2{(e)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})-2{(1)}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3})]-6{\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-6(\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =6{e}^{2}-3({e}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/example-493.json" "file_sha256" "ba7bdd5687966781ee367005e519423e48d49430fb7c40f037f14d301011c492"} {"question" "e-494" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log_4{x}}{x^3} \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/example-494.json" "file_sha256" "9016a6d021ad006469ce80377277497e771fb7d1146fd3ab93b33c246b7952f4"} {"question" "e-494" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{4}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{4}⁡x(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})-\\int (-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,{log}_{4}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(-\\,\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula $\\log_4{x}=\\dfrac{\\ln{x}}{\\ln{4}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/example-494.json" "file_sha256" "9016a6d021ad006469ce80377277497e771fb7d1146fd3ab93b33c246b7952f4"} {"question" "e-3993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/example-3993.json" "file_sha256" "670355f608cfeac1291c60ee1d1a3072a4ff53dea0836ba8bb464613fb04fd6d"} {"question" "e-3993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "At first, it may not look like we have two factors. Actually, we do, but one of them is implicit. The trick is to write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\int \\ln{x} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing this trick, we can now use integration by parts. We let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the by-parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x+C \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/example-3993.json" "file_sha256" "670355f608cfeac1291c60ee1d1a3072a4ff53dea0836ba8bb464613fb04fd6d"}] "usage" {"e-3993" [] "q-12570" [] "e-494" [] "e-493" []} "basis" 1323 "retractions" [[17592186096977 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{\\log_{3} x}{x^{3}}dx$."] [17592186096398 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{e} 4x\\ln\\left(x^3\\right) \\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186096398 :question/worked-solution "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and $v'$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = \\ln (x^{3}) & ⟹u^{′} = \\frac{1}{x^{3}} \\cdot 3x^{2} = \\frac{3}{x} \\\\ v^{′} = 4x & ⟹v = \\int4xdx = 2x^{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{1}^{e}4x\\ln (x^{3})dx &= \\int_{1}^{e}uv^{′}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.uv\\right|_{1}^{e} - \\int_{1}^{e}vu^{′}dx \\\\\n&= \\ln (x^{3}) \\cdot \\left.(2x^{2})\\right|_{1}^{e} - \\int_{1}^{e}(2x^{2}) \\cdot \\frac{3}{x}dx \\\\\n&= [2(e)^{2}\\ln (e^{3}) - 2(1)^{2}\\ln (1^{3})] - 6\\int_{1}^{e}xdx \\\\\n&= 6e^{2} - \\left.6(\\frac{1}{2}x^{2})\\right|_{1}^{e} \\\\\n&= 6e^{2} - \\left.3x^{2}\\right|_{1}^{e} \\\\\n&= 6e^{2} - 3(e^{2} - 1^{2}) \\\\\n&= 3e^{2} + 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096399 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log_4{x}}{x^3} \\,\\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186096399 :question/worked-solution "We define\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = \\log_{4} x & ⟹u^{′} = \\frac{1}{x\\ln 4} \\\\ v^{′} = \\frac{1}{x^{3}} & ⟹v = \\int\\frac{1}{x^{3}}dx =-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{\\log_{4} x}{x^{3}}dx &= \\intuv^{′}dx \\\\\n&= uv - \\intvu^{′}dx \\\\\n&= \\log_{4} x(-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}}) - \\int(-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}})\\frac{1}{x\\ln 4}dx \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}}\\log_{4} x + \\frac{1}{2\\ln 4}\\int\\frac{1}{x^{3}}dx \\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\ln x}{2x^{2}\\ln 4} + \\frac{1}{2\\ln 4}(-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}}) + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\ln x}{2x^{2}\\ln 4} - \\frac{1}{4x^{2}\\ln 4} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2\\ln x + 1}{4x^{2}\\ln 4} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula\n\n$$\n\\log_4{x}=\\dfrac{\\ln{x}}{\\ln{4}}\n$$"] [17592186096350 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x$."] [17592186096350 :question/worked-solution "At first, it may not look like we have two factors. Actually, we do, but one of them is implicit. The trick is to write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\ln{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\int \\ln{x} \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nUsing this trick, we can now use integration by parts. We let\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = \\ln x & ⟹u^{′} = \\frac{1}{x} \\\\ v^{′} = 1 & ⟹v = x\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, using the by-parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\ln xdx &= x\\ln x - \\intx \\cdot \\frac{1}{x}dx \\\\\n&= x\\ln x - \\int1dx \\\\\n&= x\\ln x - x + C \\\\\n&= x(\\ln x - 1) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186094269 17592186094270 17592186094271 17592186094272 17592186094273] "immutable_fields" [[17592186094268 :answer-field/correct] [17592186094268 :answer-field/id] [17592186094268 :answer-field/key] [17592186094268 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
